From d91a500eba3b8bc83ef6c6f0de9d8735f300827b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shreeram Ramamoorthy Swaminathan <shrerama@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Mar 2026 00:46:12 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] [GWAPPS][RDK][QMESH]: Implement JSON-based configuration and
 qmesh_cli

DESCRIPTION:
Implement a configuration backend for RDK-B using a JSON file (`/etc/config/prplmesh.json`) since UCI is not available. This includes the BPL adaptation layer, a default config generator script, and a CLI tool (`qmesh_cli`) to view and modify the configuration.

PROBLEM:
The RDK-B platform does not include the UCI (Unified Configuration Interface) system used by OpenWrt. Consequently, prplMesh cannot store or retrieve its configuration settings (like management mode, radio settings, etc.) when running on RDK-B, preventing proper operation.

ANALYSIS:
The platform abstraction layer (BPL) handles configuration access. On OpenWrt, this maps to UCI calls. On RDK-B, a different storage mechanism is required. A JSON file structure closely mirroring the existing UCI schema was selected for portability and simplicity.

FIX:
1. Created `create_rdk_default_config.sh`: A script to generate a default `/etc/config/prplmesh.json` with detected backhaul interfaces and standard defaults.
2. Implemented `framework/platform/bpl/cfg/rdk/bpl_cfg_helper.cpp`: Provides functions to read and write parameters to the JSON file using the `cJSON` library.
3. Updated `framework/platform/bpl/CMakeLists.txt`: Adjusted to compile the new helper and link against `cJSON` for the RDK-B target.
4. Added `tools/qmesh_cli`: A new C-based CLI utility (`qmesh_cli`) that supports `get`, `set`, and `show` commands to manipulate the JSON configuration, mimicking basic `uci` command functionality.
5. Updated root `CMakeLists.txt` to include the new tool in the build.

IMPACT ANALYSIS:
Design change: Yes, introduces JSON-based config storage for RDK-B.
Impacted areas: RDK-B platform builds, configuration loading sequence.
Behavior change: None for OpenWrt. RDK-B now requires `cJSON` and uses `/etc/config/prplmesh.json`.

UNIT TEST RESULTS:
- Verified successful compilation.

